WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.700
Welcome to Now You See It.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.700
When characters drown in movies, they’re
gone forever. But more than just the character

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.860
leaves. They always take something with them.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.540
Maybe they take away fear

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.220
A friendship

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:23.700
trust in others

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.760
or a desire to go somewhere new.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:29.140
But what happens when a character starts drowning
and survives?

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:33.320
He’s not gone forever, but instead, he’s
alive. But he isn’t just alive. He’s alive

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:38.050
all over again. He’s supposed to be dead.
When he rises up again, he changes. But change

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.870
isn’t the right word. It’s more violent
than change.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:42.170
He’s reborn.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.000
Let’s look at drowning more symbolically in The Truman Show.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.640
Truman lives on an island, caged from reality. He’s

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.440
been conditioned to fear the outside world
after the drowning of his father. Finally,

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.820
he sails out of his world and confronts the
next, nearly drowning in the process. It’s

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:15.110
the same pattern we see in baptism: death
and rebirth through the medium of water. Truman

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:19.900
goes in still scared of the outside world
and comes out ready. He died and was born again.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:24.760
In any drowning scene we see symbolic rebirth
which originates from the Judeo-Christian

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:30.080
sacrament of baptism: a new believer is taken
completely underwater, dies out of his old

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:33.480
self and is reborn in his identity as a follower of Christ.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:53.720
Using water as death and rebirth
imagery has been used for centuries in literature,

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.450
but it has since found its way into film.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:59.440
Every drowning experience has a different
meaning based on the context. Whoever causes

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:04.360
you to nearly drown is the symbolic enemy, and whoever saves you is your symbolic savior.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:09.820
This includes drowning yourself and saving yourself. And if you’re unable to save someone else, that

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:12.800
represents losing a part of yourself if that person was close to you.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.800
Baptism imagery is not restricted to violent
drowning. We can see the same death and rebirth,

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:22.379
more subtly, in, say, a shower scene or a
sewage drain followed by a torrential downpour.

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:26.719
While not as apparent, any scene where a character
gets cleansed with water can represent a death

00:02:26.719 --> 00:02:28.010
and rebirth for the character.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:32.749
The shower scene in Psycho has baptism imagery.
Actress Janet Leigh said in her book on the

00:02:32.749 --> 00:02:37.139
film: “Marion had decided to go back to Phoenix,
come clean, and take the consequence, so when

00:02:37.139 --> 00:02:40.920
she stepped into the bathtub it was as if
she were stepping into the baptismal waters.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:45.139
The spray beating down on her was purifying
the corruption from her mind, purging the

00:02:45.139 --> 00:02:48.810
evil from her soul. She was like a virgin
again, tranquil, at peace.”

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:52.670
In the shower, she’s cleansing herself of
her sins. In her attempt, though, she gets

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.170
murdered, and fails in her baptism.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:58.880
Countless films use water as a way
of showing a deep internal change for a character.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.840
So whenever someone goes underwater, whether
they’re hiding, feeling trapped, getting

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:07.920
super powers, or falling out of an exploding
plane, remember that getting dunked underwater

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.450
represents a part of them dying and another
part being born.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:14.299
Or maybe it’s just a way to get a kiss from
Wendy Peffercorn.

